   160	- `node --run test:coverage` passes on the committed implementation: 99.69%
   161	  statements, 98.51% branches, 98.18% functions, and 100% lines. The built-Worker
   162	  integration suite remains outside coverage instrumentation.
   163	- `git diff --check` passes. A final origin refresh still resolves to the reviewed
   164	  base. The dependency lockfile has no changes.
   165	
   166	### Standards
   167	
   168	Independent review of the committed diff found zero mandatory violations and zero
   169	actionable heuristic findings. Service and implementation documentation meet the
   170	contribution rules; terminology, trust ownership, package interfaces, and test
   171	placement are preserved. The redirect helper and shared parser keep their policies
   172	local. Independent test literals provide useful expectations without a new fixture
   173	abstraction.
   174	
   175	### Spec
   176	
   177	An independent reviewer with no implementation role found zero missing, incorrect,
   178	or out-of-scope requirements in the committed diff. Redirect behavior, incomplete
   179	diagnostics, OAuth response handling, job validation, authenticated decoding, and
   180	safe secret errors match the agreed contracts. The reviewer examined source, tests,
   181	and primary documentation, but did not independently rerun the suite or inspect
   182	production services. Report substantiation concerns were resolved by adding pinned
   183	deployment references, qualifying enforcement claims, and recording the execution
   184	evidence below.
   185	
   186	Standards: 0 findings. Spec: 0 findings. Neither axis has an outstanding source issue.
   187	
   188	### Execution evidence
